\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 1\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1 Introduction\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.1 Introduction\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Phishing is no longer limited to a plainly suspicious web address. Attackers use\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 shortened or lookalike URLs, urgent SMS messages, polished email text, copied logos,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 QR codes, and screenshots that imitate legitimate login pages. Users often have only\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 seconds to decide whether to click, reply, scan, or share a one-time password.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield is proposed as a single platform that analyzes the evidence available in\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 each of these forms and gives a cautious, understandable risk assessment before an\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 unsafe action is taken.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 evidence source, and confidence. The scoring layer removes duplicate evidence, applies\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 a transparent policy, and records the limitations of unavailable services. This separation\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 makes the behavior easier to test, protects sensitive content, and allows a future model\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 or intelligence-feed change to be reviewed without changing the entire platform.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The implementation is validated with representative benign, ambiguous, and synthetic\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 phishing samples. Acceptance evidence includes correct input validation, a stable result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 schema, explainable indicators, safe user guidance, and protected audit records. A result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 is never described as guaranteed safe: where evidence is weak, stale, or unavailable, the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interface states that uncertainty and directs the user to verify through an independently\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 known official channel.\par
\page
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 2\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1 Introduction\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.2 Aims and Objectives of the Work\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The aim of CyberShield is to create a reliable and user-oriented phishing detection\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 platform that supports URL analysis, SMS/email text analysis, and screenshot analysis.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Its objectives are to identify commonly observed phishing indicators, combine\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 cybersecurity and AI-based evidence, explain the reason for a risk level, preserve\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 privacy, support feedback, and provide a foundation for future integration with security\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 teams. The project emphasizes prevention and awareness rather than automated\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 enforcement or unverified accusation.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 evidence source, and confidence. The scoring layer removes duplicate evidence, applies\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 a transparent policy, and records the limitations of unavailable services. This separation\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 makes the behavior easier to test, protects sensitive content, and allows a future model\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 or intelligence-feed change to be reviewed without changing the entire platform.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The implementation is validated with representative benign, ambiguous, and synthetic\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 phishing samples. Acceptance evidence includes correct input validation, a stable result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 schema, explainable indicators, safe user guidance, and protected audit records. A result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 is never described as guaranteed safe: where evidence is weak, stale, or unavailable, the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interface states that uncertainty and directs the user to verify through an independently\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 known official channel.\par
\page
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 3\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1 Introduction\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.3 Brief Literature Review\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Phishing research and operational guidance consistently show that social engineering\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 succeeds by creating urgency, trust, fear, or reward. URL-based signals such as\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 deceptive domains and malicious reputation remain important, but language analysis\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 adds evidence about credential requests and impersonation. OCR and visual analysis\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 extend coverage to screenshots that conceal a destination or reproduce a trusted brand.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 This review motivates a multi-modal design in which no single weak signal is treated as\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 proof, while several corroborating signals can produce a strong warning.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 evidence source, and confidence. The scoring layer removes duplicate evidence, applies\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 a transparent policy, and records the limitations of unavailable services. This separation\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 makes the behavior easier to test, protects sensitive content, and allows a future model\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 or intelligence-feed change to be reviewed without changing the entire platform.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The implementation is validated with representative benign, ambiguous, and synthetic\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 phishing samples. Acceptance evidence includes correct input validation, a stable result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 schema, explainable indicators, safe user guidance, and protected audit records. A result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 is never described as guaranteed safe: where evidence is weak, stale, or unavailable, the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interface states that uncertainty and directs the user to verify through an independently\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 known official channel.\par
\page
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 4\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1 Introduction\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.4 Problem Definition\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Existing link checkers do not fully address the way suspicious content is shared through\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 messages and images. A user may receive a delivery SMS with a link, a fake banking\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 email without a visible URL, or a screenshot asking for an OTP. In each case, the user\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 needs a prompt assessment that identifies the relevant evidence and suggests a safe\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 response. The central problem is therefore to provide a privacy-conscious, explainable\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 analysis workflow that can interpret multiple input forms without automatically visiting\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 dangerous content or promising perfect detection.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 evidence source, and confidence. The scoring layer removes duplicate evidence, applies\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 a transparent policy, and records the limitations of unavailable services. This separation\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 makes the behavior easier to test, protects sensitive content, and allows a future model\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 or intelligence-feed change to be reviewed without changing the entire platform.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The implementation is validated with representative benign, ambiguous, and synthetic\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 phishing samples. Acceptance evidence includes correct input validation, a stable result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 schema, explainable indicators, safe user guidance, and protected audit records. A result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 is never described as guaranteed safe: where evidence is weak, stale, or unavailable, the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interface states that uncertainty and directs the user to verify through an independently\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 known official channel.\par
\page
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 5\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1 Introduction\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 1.5 Plan of the Work\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The project plan begins with requirement study and threat understanding, followed by\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 technology selection, architecture design, dataset preparation, implementation, testing,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 and documentation. URL analysis provides the initial cybersecurity layer; the NLP\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 module extends detection to SMS and email language; the image module adds OCR\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 and visual indicators for screenshots. Integration work combines results through a\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 versioned scoring policy. The final phase evaluates accuracy, usability, performance,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 security, and limitations before preparing the report and demonstration.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 evidence source, and confidence. The scoring layer removes duplicate evidence, applies\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 a transparent policy, and records the limitations of unavailable services. This separation\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 makes the behavior easier to test, protects sensitive content, and allows a future model\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 or intelligence-feed change to be reviewed without changing the entire platform.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The implementation is validated with representative benign, ambiguous, and synthetic\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 phishing samples. Acceptance evidence includes correct input validation, a stable result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 schema, explainable indicators, safe user guidance, and protected audit records. A result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 is never described as guaranteed safe: where evidence is weak, stale, or unavailable, the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interface states that uncertainty and directs the user to verify through an independently\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 known official channel.\par
\page
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 6\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2 Technology and Literature Review\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2.1 Cybersecurity Foundations\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield uses defensive cybersecurity principles: untrusted input is validated,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 suspicious URLs are never opened in the user browser, reputation lookups are\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 server-side, and results are presented as decision support. Important technical indicators\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 include host structure, top-level domain, encoding, redirect behavior, certificate-related\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 context, and threat-intelligence reputation.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 evidence source, and confidence. The scoring layer removes duplicate evidence, applies\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 a transparent policy, and records the limitations of unavailable services. This separation\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 makes the behavior easier to test, protects sensitive content, and allows a future model\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 or intelligence-feed change to be reviewed without changing the entire platform.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The implementation is validated with representative benign, ambiguous, and synthetic\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 phishing samples. Acceptance evidence includes correct input validation, a stable result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 schema, explainable indicators, safe user guidance, and protected audit records. A result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 is never described as guaranteed safe: where evidence is weak, stale, or unavailable, the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interface states that uncertainty and directs the user to verify through an independently\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 known official channel.\par
\page
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 7\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2 Technology and Literature Review\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2.2 URL Analysis Technologies\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 A URL parser separates scheme, host, path, query, port, and encoded characters.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Normalization detects misleading forms such as IP-address hosts, repeated separators,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 punycode, long subdomains, or lookalike brand names. Threat-intelligence adapters\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 enrich the normalized indicator while retaining source freshness and failure status.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 evidence source, and confidence. The scoring layer removes duplicate evidence, applies\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 a transparent policy, and records the limitations of unavailable services. This separation\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 makes the behavior easier to test, protects sensitive content, and allows a future model\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 or intelligence-feed change to be reviewed without changing the entire platform.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The implementation is validated with representative benign, ambiguous, and synthetic\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 phishing samples. Acceptance evidence includes correct input validation, a stable result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 schema, explainable indicators, safe user guidance, and protected audit records. A result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 is never described as guaranteed safe: where evidence is weak, stale, or unavailable, the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interface states that uncertainty and directs the user to verify through an independently\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 known official channel.\par
\page
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 8\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2 Technology and Literature Review\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2.3 NLP for SMS and Email\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 NLP is used to detect urgency, threats, prize claims, account-verification requests,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 credential or payment requests, sender impersonation, and unusual instructions. Entity\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 extraction identifies domains, phone numbers, email addresses, amounts, and\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 organization names. The approach combines rules and cautious classification so that\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 ordinary urgent communication is not automatically called fraud.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 evidence source, and confidence. The scoring layer removes duplicate evidence, applies\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 a transparent policy, and records the limitations of unavailable services. This separation\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 makes the behavior easier to test, protects sensitive content, and allows a future model\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 or intelligence-feed change to be reviewed without changing the entire platform.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The implementation is validated with representative benign, ambiguous, and synthetic\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 phishing samples. Acceptance evidence includes correct input validation, a stable result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 schema, explainable indicators, safe user guidance, and protected audit records. A result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 is never described as guaranteed safe: where evidence is weak, stale, or unavailable, the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interface states that uncertainty and directs the user to verify through an independently\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 known official channel.\par
\page
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 9\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2 Technology and Literature Review\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 2.4 Image Processing and OCR\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 Screenshot analysis begins with safe decoding of PNG, JPEG, or WEBP files. OCR\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 extracts visible text and confidence values; image processing identifies form-like\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 layouts, QR codes, login prompts, payment prompts, and logo-like patterns. Extracted\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 text is passed to the NLP service, while visual signals remain distinct in the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 explanation.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
