\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield - Project Report\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 13\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 3 System Requirements Study\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 3.1 User Characteristics\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield serves different user groups with different information needs. A guest can\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 submit a limited analysis and see the immediate result. A registered user can manage\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 history and consent. An analyst reviews authorized flagged cases and provides\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 disposition. An administrator configures limits, policies, roles, and integrations. An\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 auditor reviews permitted governance events. Role separation reduces exposure of raw\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 content and ensures that users see only the information required for their tasks.\par
