\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 3 System Requirements Study\b0\fs24\par
\pard\sb240\sa140\b\fs32 3.12 Assumptions and Dependencies\b0\fs24\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield assumes that users submit material they are authorized to inspect and that\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 external intelligence providers can be delayed, unavailable, or incomplete. OCR quality\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 depends on image resolution, language, compression, and layout. The system depends\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 on authentication, storage, database backup, reputation adapters, OCR capability, and\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 monitoring. Each dependency is isolated so that a known limitation can be reported\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 honestly.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 CyberShield treats this capability as a controlled pipeline rather than a single\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 prediction. Input is validated, normalized, and routed only to the services required for\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 the selected modality. Each analyzer returns versioned indicators with severity,\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 evidence source, and confidence. The scoring layer removes duplicate evidence, applies\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 a transparent policy, and records the limitations of unavailable services. This separation\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 makes the behavior easier to test, protects sensitive content, and allows a future model\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 or intelligence-feed change to be reviewed without changing the entire platform.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The implementation is validated with representative benign, ambiguous, and synthetic\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 phishing samples. Acceptance evidence includes correct input validation, a stable result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 schema, explainable indicators, safe user guidance, and protected audit records. A result\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 is never described as guaranteed safe: where evidence is weak, stale, or unavailable, the\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 interface states that uncertainty and directs the user to verify through an independently\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 known official channel.\par
