\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The context model shows that users interact through the browser client, while protected\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 services perform URL, text, and image analysis. External intelligence is accessed by\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 server-side adapters, not directly from the browser.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 The diagram is a logical representation intended to support implementation and testing.\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 It identifies responsibility and data movement without locking the project to a specific\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 framework or vendor. Trust boundaries remain between the browser, API, worker\par
\pard\qj\sa120\sl360\slmult1 processes, external intelligence providers, and protected storage.\par
